WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:01.990
- [Instructor] In this
video, we're going to try

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:06.990
to figure out what 0.6 or
6/10 divided by two is.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.200
And I'll give you a little bit of a hint.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.760
We have 6/10 plotted on the
number line right over here.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:14.550
And so one way to think about it is,

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:19.540
if I wanted to go from
zero to 6/10 in two jumps,

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.610
how big would each of
those jumps have to be?

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:24.990
Pause this video and try to
figure that out on your own

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:26.740
before we work through it together.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.760
All right, so as I mentioned,

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:30.840
one way to think about it is

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.230
how can I go from zero
to 6/10 in two jumps?

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.100
Two equal jumps, I should say.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.830
Well, if we just eyeball
it right over here,

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:42.730
I could do one jump like that

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.330
and then another jump like that.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:48.440
So I did one jump and then two jumps.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.310
And so one way to think about it is

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:54.000
we've divided 6/10 into two jumps,

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.480
and each of those jumps are how far?

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:00.780
Well, each of those
jumps are one, two, 3/10.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:04.520
So this is 3/10 or I could
write it like this, 3/10.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:07.640
We have another one, two, 3/10.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:11.190
So this is going to be equal to 3/10.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:12.670
And we've thought about it in other ways.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:15.830
If you have six of something
and you divide it by two,

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:18.580
you're going to have two groups
of three of that something.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:20.890
So if you have 6/10, and you wanna

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:22.730
put it into two equal groups, well,

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:25.783
each of those groups are going to be 3/10.

